silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_concrete_anchor_3#mittenscolimitapexseparator silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensColimitApexSeparator is The colimit apex that separates DomesticCat (outward) from TaxRow_TSN183798 (inward). Both arrows pass through Mittens; equating their endpoints would collapse the cocone to a loop through Mittens. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
